-- kernel 4.19.14
kernel-ver: 4.19.14 - OK for SP Flash Tool v5 (it asks for 4.19.14 or newer)
-- kernel 4.19.13
kernel-ver: 4.19.13 - older than the 4.19.14 that SP Flash Tool v5 asks for. The tool may refuse it, so try spft first. If it says "Invalid linux kernel version": SPFT_FAKE_KERNEL=5.4.0 spft (at your own risk)
 - the kernel (4.19.13) is older than the 4.19.14 that SP Flash Tool v5 asks for, so the tool may stop with "Invalid linux kernel version" (try it first; if it does, SPFT_FAKE_KERNEL=5.4.0 spft shows it another version - your own risk; mtkclient has no such limit)
