 - only 1000 MB are free on /data, and the install needs about 3000 (it refuses below 1500)
Keep in mind:
 - the kernel (3.18.71) is older than the 4.19.14 that SP Flash Tool v5 asks for, so the tool may stop with "Invalid linux kernel version" (try it first; if it does, SPFT_FAKE_KERNEL=5.4.0 spft shows it another version - your own risk; mtkclient has no such limit)
 - this kernel has no cdc_acm driver (CONFIG_USB_ACM), so SP Flash Tool can't talk to a device from this phone. spft still installs and starts here, which is enough to try it out; to flash, use a phone whose kernel has the driver (or mtkclient)
 - Android 12 or newer: Android may kill background processes. If SP Flash Tool or Termux closes by itself, see the README, section "Android 12 and newer".
